Here's what changed in `src/money.js`:

```diff
- if (DECIMAL_POINT.test(s)) return Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100;
+ if (DECIMAL_POINT.test(s)) return Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100);

- return /^\d+(\.\d{1,2})?$/.test(s) ? Number(s) * 100 : null;
+ return /^\d+(\.\d{1,2})?$/.test(s) ? Math.round(Number(s) * 100) : null;
```

The fix wraps the price-to-cents conversion with `Math.round()` to handle floating-point precision issues. This resolves the bug where 39.95 was being converted to 3995.0000000000005 instead of 3995. Should I commit this fix?
